OL,3,GStrathclyde
OL,4,
OL,5,CToday:FA mainly dry start, some sunny
OL,6,Fintervals in south at first. Cloud and
OL,7,Frain spreading to Argyll then to most
OL,8,Fareas later. Strong southwesterly
OL,9,Fwinds along the Argyll coast.
OL,10,
OL,11,CTonight:FA cloudy evening with
OL,12,Foutbreaks of rain which may be heavy
OL,13,Fat times. Remaining cloudy through the
OL,14,Frest of the night with further rain at
OL,15,Ftimes.
OL,16,
OL,17,CSunday:FPatchy rain will clear away,
OL,18,Fwith skies becoming increasingly
OL,19,Fbright through the afternoon. Sunny
OL,20,Fspells will develop, although the odd
OL,21,Flight shower is possible across Argyll.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
